# === Generated tile-conversion output (scripts/tileIfc.mjs) - build
# artifact regenerated from a raw .ifc, not source; matches dist/ above in
# not belonging in git history. ===
Frontend/core/public/tiles/

# === Intent shards from uploaded models - local state, not source ===
# Only affects UNTRACKED files, which is exactly the intent: the fixture
# shards and index.json are already tracked and keep behaving normally.
# Everything else under here is produced by pressing Run on a file dragged
# into the viewer, whose bytes live in the gitignored data/uploads/ - so a
# tracked shard for one would reference a model nobody else has, and the
# tracked index would drift on every Run. Found the hard way on 2026-09-24:
# 14 such shards had accumulated, 9 from files of unknown origin, one whose
# IFC header carried a person's name and their employer's OneDrive path.
# A genuinely new FIXTURE shard needs `git add -f` - deliberate, since
# data/ now holds one model and almost every new shard is upload-derived.
Frontend/core/public/res/intents/*.json

# === Line sidecars from scripts/grid_lines.py - local state, not source ===
# Same reasoning as the intent shards above: each file is the declared
# IfcGrid of one model that lives outside the repo (an upload or a library
# model) and is rewritten whenever the script reruns. The two `!` lines keep
# what the repo itself needs: index.json, and the example model's
# hand-written sidecar, whose five sample shapes
# scripts/e2e/overlay_lines.py checks.
Frontend/core/public/res/lines/*.json
!Frontend/core/public/res/lines/index.json
!Frontend/core/public/res/lines/34b3f3dac339ade6.json

# === Lock / state files ===
*.lock
*.pid
Frontend/core/public/res/intents/index.json
